      :sym "architecture/wasm-core-substrate"
      :title "Universal WebAssembly Ambient Substrate, Self-Contained Micro-Binary Packaging, and Regulated Platform Leaves Standard"
      :intent "Establish WebAssembly as universal ambient execution plane and primary compilation target, package minimal self-contained CLI binary without Rust tax, and regulate lateral targets under strict unidirectional export boundaries"
      :outcome "Universal cross-platform WASM deployment across browsers, servers, and micro-runtimes with minimal <1.5MB native binary and formal regulation of Rust, Go, C, and Mobile UI platform leaves"
      :whyNot ("Treating WebAssembly as a secondary target and relying on heavyweight foreign language toolchains creates context bloat, impedance mismatch, and impairs self-hosting sovereignty")
