     (:id "d78"
      :sym "architecture/cross-platform-wasm-core-and-browser-runtime"
      :title "Cross-Platform WebAssembly Core Substrate, Browser Autonomous Runtime, and Native Engine Micro-Evaluation"
      :intent "Eradicate Apple-proprietary JavaScriptCore dependency from asl-eval, consolidate cross-platform evaluation into native engine, package sovereign asl-core.wasm (<150 KB) for in-browser autonomous execution with in-memory VFS and zero-socket Batch RPC, and prioritize C99 engine rewrite as the final migration phase"
      :outcome "Universal cross-platform evaluation across Linux, Windows, and macOS; fully autonomous browser agent execution under 16 MB RSS; and structured phased deferral of C source rewrite"
      :whyNot ("Relying on macOS-proprietary frameworks blocks Linux/Windows execution, and premature engine rewriting risks monorepo stability before WASM substrate and browser contracts are solidified")
      :adr ".asl/mem/decisions/D78CrossPlatformWasmCoreAndBrowserRuntime.asn"
