     (:id "d79"
      :sym "architecture/sovereign-single-binary-asl-consolidation"
      :title "Sovereign Single-Binary ASL Consolidation: Unifying Engine, Eval, Compiler, Evolver, and Memory into a Self-Contained Dependency-Free Executable"
      :intent "Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078)."
      :outcome "Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078); complete elimination of asl-engine and asl-eval binary sprawl; pruning of the 7389-line shell script; and pristine isolation of database and external drivers"
      :whyNot ("Maintaining separate daemon/eval binaries causes process fragmentation, and leaving the 7389-line script retains 3319 lines of unreadable transliterator bloat")
      :adr ".asl/mem/decisions/D79SovereignSingleBinaryAslConsolidation.asn"
      :tasks [
        "Task43401"
        "Task43402"
        "Task43403"
        "Task43404"
        "Task43405"
        "Task43406"
      ]
      :closure "When sovereign single-binary is superseded by modular microVM distribution"
      :status "active")

     (:id "d80"
      :sym "architecture/context-aware-hierarchical-workspace-visibility-topology"
      :title "Context-Aware Hierarchical Workspace and Worktree Visibility Topology"
      :intent "Enforce strict 3-tier visibility rules: unanchored sessions see only their own session, workspace sessions see only their active workspace and derived child worktrees, and panoptic system visibility is unlocked strictly from the directory containing the global .asl store"
      :outcome "Elimination of cross-project context pollution, prompt bloat, and accidental cross-repo mutations; pure algorithmic resolution in asl-mem/visibility-scope; and physical location gating for whole-system discovery"
      :whyNot ("Flat visibility causes severe prompt bloat and cross-repo hallucinations in multi-project orchestrations")
      :adr ".asl/mem/decisions/D80HierarchicalWorkspaceVisibilityAndSovereignDiscoveryTopology.asn"
      :tasks [
        "Task43501"
        "Task43502"
        "Task43503"
        "Task43504"
      ]
      :closure "When hierarchical worktree visibility is superseded by ambient virtual workspace federation"
      :status "active")
     (:id "d81"
      :sym "architecture/language-ground-truth-and-sovereign-portability-program"
      :title "Owned ASL Semantics, Portable Native/WASM Tooling and Autonomous Self-Hosting"
      :intent "Settle six ordered phases: Phase436 semantics and honest verification; Phase437 canonical rule/client projections; Phase438 observable portable native/WASM core and truthful batches; Phase439 independent production-fault, cost and claim evidence; Phase440 autonomous ASL native compiler/evaluator stage2 rebuild and all tooling; Phase441 attention/session isolation and measured compression. Task dependency edges govern scheduling; serialize overlapping writers. Existing tasks are amended rather than duplicated; runtime implementation and behavioral baselines remain pending."
      :outcome "Observable semantic conformance, genuine fault-sensitive independent gates and source-bound receipts; autonomous native compiler/evaluator/adapter stage2 rebuild with a WASM backend and Darwin/Linux/Windows contracts; measured cost per correct task and constraint-preserving handoff. Plan agreement is separate from implementation completion."
      :whyNot ("Output labels, assertion-count parity and an externally executed WASM file do not establish the owned self-hosted tool or its reliability.")
