     (:id "d83"
      :sym "architecture/rpc-first-record-store-and-attention-separation"
      :title "RPC-First Record Store, Attention Separation, and Event-Driven Memory Architecture"
      :intent "Transition all monorepo records (tasks, decisions, receipts, plans, phases, telemetry, component docs, intents, notes, principles, recipes) from raw direct file writes to an RPC-first contract engine with attention separation, deterministic VFS serialization, pluggable storage adapters, and agentic observability event streaming"
      :outcome "Elimination of delimiter corruption, agent context protection via sub-80 token blamed rejection receipts, deterministic C-enforced indentation and comment-free serialization, flock concurrency safety across subagents, and zero-polling event streams for live dashboards and remote integrations"
      :whyNot ("Direct file writing causes severe cognitive attention dispersal, race conditions on shared files, and context blowout on post-factum syntax errors")
      :adr ".asl/mem/decisions/D83RpcRecordStoreAndDeterministicDistribution.asn"
      :tasks [
        "Task48401"
